You are given a 4-bit adder module that takes two 4-bit inputs, `A` and `B`, and outputs the sum in a 4-bit output `S`. Your task is to implement a verilog module that uses the adder module to perform a 8-bit addition. The module should take two 8-bit inputs, `A` and `B`, and output the sum in a 8-bit output `S`. You should use the `\$xor` module to implement the adder module.

Assume that the `\$xor` module has the following interface:
```
module \$xor (input a, input b, output s);
endmodule
```
You can use the `\$xor` module to implement the 4-bit adder module as follows:
```
module adder4(input [3:0] A, input [3:0] B, output [3:0] S);
    wire c1, c2, c3;
    \$xor x1(.a(A[0]), .b(B[0]), .s(S[0]));
    \$xor x2(.a(A[1]), .b(B[1]), .s(S[1]));
    \$xor x3(.a(A[2]), .b(B[2]), .s(S[2]));
    \$xor x4(.a(A[3]), .b(B[3]), .s(S[3]));
    \$xor x5(.a(c1), .b(S[0]), .s(c2));
    \$xor x6(.a(c2), .b(S[1]), .s(c3));
    \$xor x7(.a(c3), .b(S[2]), .s(S[3]));
endmodule
```
You are not allowed to use any other verilog module or operators to implement the 8-bit adder module.

